    loreSignificance: "Boba Fett's armor is the face of Mandalorian aesthetic cool in the saga — it made every viewer who saw The Empire Strikes Back want to be a bounty hunter. The irony of his non-Mandalorian status (he was a clone, not born into the culture) has been a point of contention for years, addressed in The Book of Boba Fett where he is re-forged into Mandalorian custom by the Armorer on Din Djarin's covert. His armor is a family heirloom, a survival tool, and a walking advertisement — the most recognizable Mandalorian armor in the galaxy.",
